 7689+7EEB              ;63) prints error message, IN=register C=error number, OUT=print output, then returns to the main program
 7690+7EEB              ;may be called at any time from any place
 7691+7EEB              ;if "error_handler" called, it jumps to the highest level, if "display_error" is called, it returns,
 7692+7EEB              ;to from where it has been called
 7693+7EEB              ;3 types:
 7694+7EEB              ;display_error=		only displays error number from C input an returns with carry
 7695+7EEB              ;error_handler=		displays error and jumps to error_handler_loop
 7696+7EEB              ;error_handler1=	only jumps to error handler loop
